    "title": "Suspect identified in West Valley City officer-involved shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Amelia Hobson ,\n8 hours ago\nWEST VALLEY CITY, Utah ( ABC4 ) — Law enforcement has identified the suspect they took into custody after an officer-involved shooting .\nAccording to the West Valley City Police Department (WVCPD), the suspect they took into custody is 25-year-old Stephen Lopez.\nLopez had been asked to leave a nearby homeless shelter that he was staying in and then used his vehicle to ram into an officer’s vehicle at around 9:30 a.m. on Wednesday. The responding officer fired shots at Lopez’s vehicle.\nLopez was not hit and fled the scene, before returning to the shelter parking lot, where he was taken into custody.\nOne person in custody following officer involved shooting in West Valley City WVCPD says Lopez has been booked for aggravated assault (a third-degree felony), theft of a motor vehicle (second-degree felony), failure to stop (third-degree felony), and an accident (Class A Misdemeanor).\nThe investigation is still ongoing, and law enforcement has not released any additional information at this time.\nLatest headlines: Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC4 Utah.\n3",
